/E (Artificial intelligence is rapidly transforming the way people think, behave, and interact, often in ways that are not fully understood or controlled. From influencing decision-making through algorithmic recommendations to shaping social perceptions and mental well-being, AI systems can create unintended psychological, social, and ethical consequences. These effects include over-reliance on automated systems, reduced critical thinking, bias reinforcement, and the spread of misinformation.)
